  "verdict": "METAL_OUT_CANNOT_TEST_THE_LEVER",
  "caveats": [
    "On metal_out the held-out metal has no supported pair by construction, so v_held = 0 and the stage-2 term is exactly zero. The frozen gate therefore measures stage 1 against stage 1. That is a property of the protocol, not a result about the two-stage model; the within_metal block is the informative test.",
    "The two-stage arm is evaluated against the same additive stage 1 it is built on, so its gain is bounded by how much residual structure a rank-1 ligand projection can capture. It is not a claim about the ceiling.",
    "v_m is a fixed unit vector given the supported pairs, not a fitted quantity. With one supported pair inside a training fold it is (+0.5, -0.5) exactly; the only fitted object is the 2048-dimensional ligand projection.",
    "lambda is a single closed-form shrinkage on the training pair differences; it is not cross-validated, so a small positive lambda is weak evidence of a real interaction rather than of ridge under-fitting.",
    "Stage-2 residuals are out-of-fold, which removes in-sample overfit but also shrinks them; a real interaction will appear smaller than it is."
  ],
  "elapsed_seconds": 395.0
